      "message": "in C++ stack variable might not be zero initialized, hence even if some existing_uuids are not read from config storage, its value might not be zero and uuid.IsEmpty() would fail\n\nHence, we should always zero the array to make sure that if uuids are not filled by `btif_get_existing_uuids` it is zero. \n\nFor example:\n\n```\nUuid existing_uuids[BT_MAX_NUM_UUIDS] \u003d {};\n```\n\nOr if we know how many UUIDs are read while doing `btif_get_existing_uuids`, we can loop until that limit, too",
